menu "Diagnostics commands (serial and BLE)"

    config DIAG_REBOOT_GUARD_TIMEOUT_MS
        int "Reboot guard total timeout (ms)"
        range 500 1200
        default 1000
        help
            REQ-FUNC-29/31, tech_spec.md 2.4.4. Total bound of the
            ble_host_exec() round trip that atomically checks "no OTA in
            flight". 350 ms of it is the completion window; the rest is the
            window for the host task to start the check, sized against the
            worst-case OTA RX callback of about 350 ms. The 1200 ms cap
            keeps esp_restart() within 1440 ms of the command, inside the
            1.5 s bound.

    config DIAG_REBOOT_ACK_WAIT_MS
        int "Maximum wait for the reboot acknowledgement to leave the device (ms)"
        range 100 1000
        default 1000
        help
            OQ-12. The actual wait is further limited by the single
            command deadline (command time + 1410 ms).

    config DIAG_ACCEL_TASK_STACK
        int "accel_xyz session task stack (bytes)"
        default 3072
        help
            REQ-MEM-04. Initial value; resize from the measured STACK_HWM.
            Allocated on the heap once at init.

    config DIAG_ACCEL_TASK_PRIO
        int "accel_xyz session task priority"
        range 1 10
        default 4
        help
            Above the BLE CLI worker (3) so slot deadlines are not delayed
            by response handling, below the BLE host (21) and controller (23).
            REQ-PERF-02.

endmenu
